  "details": "TLDR :\n\nWhen playing on VRC on Quest, the in-game text boxes do not detect inputs from bluetooth keyboards.\n\nTo reproduce the experiment :\n\n1. From Quest (tested on 3 and 3s), link your headset with a compatible bluetooth keyboard (tested on Anker Ultra-Compact A7726, Logitech MX Keys S, and Logitech Unify keyboards). \n\n2. Launch VRChat from the Quest headset.\n\n3. For any text inputs (log-in, search, chatbox), use the keyboard to type.\n\nWhat happens:\n\n- The keyboard works in the game, even while browsing other apps in the meantime. The game detects the keyboard, as I can move (WASD), rotate (, .), open the menu (esc) and the contextual menu (R), only the text inputs (chatbox, log in, search) don't.\n\n- Although I could move, rotate and interact in game with our keyboard, I couldn't use the keyboard anymore unless exiting out of the chatbox keyboard input.\n\nConclusion:\n\n- Fixing this bug would benefit overall VR experience for Android Quest users.",
